<title>GERMANY: Krupp profit slumps.</title>
<headline>Krupp profit slumps.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German steel and engineering group Fried. Krupp AG  Hoesch-Krupp said Wednesday its net profit dropped 59 percent last year but said it expected its results to improve in 1997.</p>
<p>Profits fell to 208 million marks ($121.7 million) last year from 505 million marks ($295 million) in 1995.</p>
<p>Group sales, however, rose slightly, to 24 billion marks ($14.04 billion) from 23.5 billion marks ($13.75 billion).</p>
<p>It said all its divisions but steel achieved a positive result on ordinary activities in 1996. The rise in sales was due to the first-time consolidation of units AST, Uhde and Bachmann.</p>
